 ### [Explicit Radiance Fields](806-explicit-radiance-fields.md)
-Explicit Radiance Fields (PERF) is a method for image-based 3D reconstruction that formulates volumetric reconstruction as a non-linear least-squares problem solved explicitly without neural networks. It uses a voxel grid for the foreground and a hierarchy of environment maps for the background, optimizing color and opacity values directly via a Gauss-Newton solver. Unlike [Plenoxels](7440-plenoxels.md) which uses neural networks for view-dependent color, PERF assumes diffuse surfaces and achieves significantly faster convergence by leveraging analytical gradients and iterative linear solvers. See [Explicit Radiance Fields](806-explicit-radiance-fields.md).
