 ### [Plenoxels Optimization Configuration](929-plenoxels-optimization-configuration.md)
-Plenoxels Optimization Configuration defines the specific hyperparameter settings and learning rate schedules required to train a static voxel grid with spherical harmonics (SH) coefficients, as introduced in the Plenoxels method. It solves the problem of efficiently optimizing high-dimensional SH coefficients and voxel opacities ($\sigma$) without the computational overhead of neural network backpropagation. It is distinguished from [PlenOctree Optimization](1291-plenoctree-optimization.md) by its use of a fixed-resolution dense or sparse voxel grid rather than a hierarchical octree, and from [Coarse-to-Fine Optimization with Pruning](1153-coarse-to-fine-optimization-with-pruning.md) by its reliance on specific optimizer choices (RMSProp) and delayed learning rate schedules rather than geometric pruning strategies. See [Plenoxels Optimization Configuration](929-plenoxels-optimization-configuration.md).
