 ### [Coarse-to-Fine Optimization with Pruning](1153-coarse-to-fine-optimization-with-pruning.md)
-Coarse-to-Fine Optimization with Pruning is a hierarchical training strategy for 3D radiance fields represented as voxel grids. It solves the problem of efficiently initializing and refining high-resolution scene representations by starting with a coarse dense grid, pruning unoccupied regions, and iteratively subdividing the remaining voxels to higher resolutions. It sets itself apart from static grid methods by dynamically adapting the voxel structure to scene complexity during training, building on the general framework of [Hierarchical Grid Optimization](1414-hierarchical-grid-optimization.md). See [Coarse-to-Fine Optimization with Pruning](1153-coarse-to-fine-optimization-with-pruning.md).
