 ### [PlenOctree Optimization](1291-plenoctree-optimization.md)
-PlenOctree Optimization is a post-training refinement process that finetunes a converted PlenOctree on original training images using Stochastic Gradient Descent (SGD) to improve image quality. It solves the residual approximation errors introduced during the conversion from a neural network to a sparse voxel grid. Unlike [Plenoxels Optimization Configuration](929-plenoxels-optimization-configuration.md), which configures fixed grid parameters, PlenOctree Optimization actively adjusts the density and spherical harmonic coefficients of the octree leaves. It also differs from [Coarse-to-Fine Optimization with Pruning](1153-coarse-to-fine-with-pruning.md) by operating on a pre-converted sparse structure rather than optimizing the network and sparsity simultaneously. See [PlenOctree Optimization](1291-plenoctree-optimization.md).
