 ### [Sparse Voxel Grid Optimization](2568-sparse-voxel-grid-optimization.md)
-Sparse Voxel Grid Optimization is a differentiable volume rendering method that optimizes a sparse 3D voxel grid for density and color features, enabling real-time high-fidelity radiance field reconstruction. It distinguishes itself from hierarchical methods like [Hierarchical Grid Optimization](1414-hierarchical-grid-optimization.md) by avoiding complex multi-resolution tree structures, instead relying on efficient occupancy caching, Morton code sorting, and near-camera voxel masking to handle unbounded scenes and accelerate training. It builds on the standard emission-absorption model and differentiability principles defined in [Hierarchical Grid Optimization](1414-hierarchical-grid-optimization.md). See [Sparse Voxel Grid Optimization](2568-sparse-voxel-grid-optimization.md).
